  "title": "Datacentres' Growth and Environmental Impact",
  "summary": "The US and China are increasing their reliance on fossil fuels to power AI growth, leading to significant carbon emissions, as highlighted by a report from the International Energy Agency (IEA). The report predicts datacentres will consume twice as much electricity by 2030 as today.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The IEA reports that datacentres will consume twice as much electricity by 2030 compared with today.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The global expansion of artificial intelligence is responsible for three-quarters of this growth.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The US and China are turning to fossil fuels to power AI growth, which is causing increased carbon emissions.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
