    {
      "title": "Datacentres to create 70% more carbon emissions by 2030, IEA report warns",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/19/datacentres-to-create-70-more-carbon-emissions-by-2030-iea-report-warns",
      "description": "<p>Global energy watchdog forecasts huge rise as US and China turn to fossil fuels to power AI growth agendas  </p><p>The world’s datacentres will create 70% more carbon emissions within the next four years as the US and China turn to fossil fuels to power their AI growth agendas, according to the world’s energy watchdog.</p><p>The International Energy Agency (IEA) warned that datacentres will consume twice as much electricity by 2030 compared with today, with the global expansion of artificial intelligence accounting for three-quarters of this growth.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/19/datacentres-to-create-70-more-carbon-emissions-by-2030-iea-report-warns\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-19T05:00:18"
    },
    {
      "title": "Data center electricity use could double by 2030, IEA says",
      "link": "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/19/data-center-electricity-demand-iea.html",
      "description": "Global electricity use by data centers could double by 2030 as the AI boom adds pressure to power grids across the world, according to the IEA.",
      "source_name": "CNBC Top News",
      "published": "2026-11-19T11:34:24"
    }
